<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a flexible conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A portable conveyor on a scissor (accordion) frame that extends, retracts, and curves. Types include gravity skatewheel, gravity roller, and powered roller. Many models expand to about four times their compressed length for truck loading, staging, and temporary operations. See our <a href="/conveyor-types/">conveyor types guide</a>.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">Skatewheel vs powered flex, which is better?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Skatewheel flex conveyors use unpowered wheels and rely on a slight decline or manual pushing. Powered flex conveyors have motorized rollers that drive products on level runs and inclines. Skatewheel units cost less and are lighter. Powered units cost more because they add motors, drive components, electrical controls, and a heavier frame.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">How long can a flexible conveyor extend?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Extended length depends on the model. Several manufacturers rate their skatewheel units to expand to about four times the compressed length. Ashland lists FlexExtend skatewheel models from 8 ft 10 in to 32 ft 5 in extended, and FMH Conveyors lists BestFlex powered units at 24, 36, and 40 ft extended. Choose a length that reaches the deepest point in the trailer you load while leaving working room for the operator.</p>

</div>
</div>
